// Code generated by forge. DO NOT EDIT.
// forge-owned: regenerated every run — do not edit (forge project disown to take ownership)
//
// PROVENANCE for this frontend's mock fixtures: which schema they were
// generated from, and where that schema lives.
//
// The fixtures in `src/mocks/<entity>_gen.ts` are a snapshot of the dev
// database's first rows, computed by applying `db/migrations` to a real
// postgres at `forge generate` time. Nothing at RUNTIME can recompute them —
// a browser has no database, and neither does `npm test` — so they are a
// cache, and this module is the cache's validity tag.
//
// `fixture-freshness_gen.test.ts` re-derives the fingerprint from the files on
// disk and compares it to the value below. That is what makes "someone edited
// a migration and forgot to re-run `forge generate`" a test failure instead of
// a set of fixtures quietly describing a schema that no longer exists.

/**
 * The digest of the input FILES these fixtures were generated from:
 * `db/migrations/*.up.sql` and `db/seeds/vocab.yaml`.
 *
 * This is the value the freshness guard recomputes, and it covers only files
 * on purpose — a vitest process can read files and nothing else. The seed
 * config lives in SEED_CONFIG_FINGERPRINT below.
 *
 * The empty string means forge recorded no fingerprint — either the project
 * has no migrations, or the inputs could not be read when the fixtures were
 * written. It is NOT a wildcard: the freshness guard treats it as "cannot
 * verify" and fails rather than passing on absent evidence.
 */
export const SEED_FINGERPRINT = "{{ .SeedFingerprint }}";

/**
 * The same digest with the seed config — salt and row counts, from
 * forge.yaml's `database.seed` block — folded in.
 *
 * Those settings reshuffle every seeded value without touching a migration,
 * so SEED_FINGERPRINT alone cannot see them change. Nothing at `npm test`
 * time can read forge.yaml's resolved seed config, so this is not what the
 * guard compares; it is recorded for `forge generate` and for anyone asking
 * which dataset a given set of fixtures came from.
 */
export const SEED_CONFIG_FINGERPRINT = "{{ .SeedConfigFingerprint }}";

/**
 * How many input files the fingerprint covers.
 *
 * A guard that asserted on a digest built from zero files would prove nothing,
 * so the count is carried alongside it and checked.
 */
export const SEED_FINGERPRINT_FILES = {{ .SeedFingerprintFiles }};

/**
 * Relative path from `src/mocks/` back to the project root — the directory
 * holding `db/migrations` and `forge.yaml`.
 *
 * Emitted rather than hardcoded because a frontend's depth is the user's
 * choice: `frontends/web` is the default, but `forge.yaml` can place one
 * anywhere, and a wrong number of `..` segments would make the freshness guard
 * silently find no migrations and pass.
 */
export const PROJECT_ROOT_FROM_FRONTEND = "{{ .ProjectRootRelative }}";
